  partName: Bolt (8)
  description: The Bolt (8) is a tiny, compact fastener positioned at the top-center-center
    of the engine, made of Material.002, playing a vital role in securing engine
    components together, maintaining the engine's structural integrity, and its compact
    shape enables efficient use of space. The Bolt (8) is designed to withstand significant
    torque forces and its central position allows for easy access for maintenance
    and repairs. Interestingly, the Bolt (8) is often used in conjunction with other
    fasteners to provide added stability and security.
